  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Module Booklets",
    "overview": "Preparation is presented as a stack of numbered, colour-coded study modules, like the coaching booklets students already worked through. A committed cobalt rail holds the navigation on a cool practice-sheet white ground (ink navy in dark). Each skill cluster owns one flat module hue, and that hue follows the skill everywhere it appears: the numbered spine of a gap or plan row, the swatch in a chip, the bar in a supply chart. One more hue, violet, is held back for a single job: marking the one step the student should take next.\n\nThe system is dense and operational: small sentence-case type, bordered flat cards, full tables for staff, and numbers that line up because every figure is tabular. Depth comes from borders and tonal surfaces. Shadows appear only on layers that float (toasts, tooltips, menus, dialogs, the active theme segment, the auth card). Motion is short and functional: state transitions, a toast slide, meters filling on mount, a press scale on buttons. All of it collapses under reduced motion.\n\nThe build rejects the grey card dashboard with one indigo accent, gradients and glow, a neon dark-only look, and gamification. Light and dark are equal citizens: every colour token carries both values through `light-dark()`.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Committed cobalt shell rail, full page height, white active pill.",
      "Five flat module hues mapped from skill clusters; violet reserved for \"next\".",
      "Numbered 44px module spines on gaps, plan items and steps.",
      "KPI tiles tied to a module by a 4px top band.",
      "One family (Geist), tabular numerals on body.",
      "Status is always icon plus label, never colour alone.",
      "Eligibility and readiness always rendered as separate blocks."
    ],
