        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Module Hue Rule",
        "body": "A skill's colour comes from its cluster through `hueFor()`, never chosen per screen.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Flat Colour Rule",
        "body": "Fills are solid tokens; no gradients and no glow anywhere.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Tabular Rule",
        "body": "The body sets `font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums`, and tables, number inputs and `time` repeat it, so every column of figures lines up.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Sentence Case Rule",
        "body": "Labels, titles and KPI captions are sentence case; uppercase belongs to the NEXT tag alone.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Two Blocks Rule",
        "body": "Eligibility and readiness are always separate cards with separate badges, and never merge into one score or block.",
        "section": "layout"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Floating-Only Shadow Rule",
        "body": "Only floating layers cast a shadow; in-flow content is bordered and flat.",
        "section": "elevation"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Top Band Rule",
        "body": "A KPI tile shows its module hue as a 4px band across the top edge; coloured side borders thicker than 1px are not used. The module spine is a numbered fill cell, not a border.",
